// Ravana — yuddha kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Yuddha Kanda, sargas 102-108 (verify)
// Migrated from the old script format. Not yet staged for the Ramlila stage.

>> scene battlefield style=kachni
>> music lanka
>> cast rama:exile at 0.36 mode=colour
>> cast agastya at 0.62 face=left mode=colour
Rama stands on the field, tired, thinking. The sage Agastya has come to watch the battle with the gods. He walks over.
AGASTYA: Listen. There is an old prayer to the Sun, the heart of Aditya. Say it three times, facing him. It ends fear.
>> pose rama namaste
>> sound bell
>> wait 1
Rama says it. The Sun, looking down, says one word: hurry.
>> exit agastya to right nowait
>> prop ch indraChariot at 0.68 raw=true dir=-1
>> enter matali from right to 0.84 in 1 colour=true
MATALI: Indra sends you his chariot, his armour and his spear. You should not meet him on foot. I am Matali. I will drive.
>> pose rama stand
>> battle ravana
-> END
